Okay.

28
00:01:15.901 --> 00:01:17.033
- Oh. my God.

29
00:01:17.077 --> 00:01:18.252
[dramatic music]

30
00:01:18.295 --> 00:01:19.688
What the hell's--
oh. my God!

31
00:01:19.731 --> 00:01:20.863
- Run!

32
00:01:20.906 --> 00:01:23.822
[overlapping screams]

33
00:01:27.478 --> 00:01:30.438
- [whimpering]

34
00:01:30.481 --> 00:01:34.181
[tense music]

35
00:01:34.572 --> 00:01:36.008
- Well. we're glad
you're here. Tiffany.

36
00:01:36.052 --> 00:01:37.532
- I'm glad to be here.

37
00:01:37.575 --> 00:01:38.837
White Collar was fun and all.

38
00:01:38.881 --> 00:01:41.101
but I didn't join the FBIto arrest accountants.

39
00:01:41.144 --> 00:01:42.537
- [chuckling]
Right.

40
00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:44.713
- By the way. what kind of nameis "Jubal"?

41
00:01:44.756 --> 00:01:47.455
- "Jubal." it is--
well. it's. I guess a tribute

42
00:01:47.498 --> 00:01:50.458
to my grandfather. theHonorable Jubal N. Valentine.

43
00:01:50.501 --> 00:01:53.156
- Oh. it's like that.

44
00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:54.462
- [chuckles]
Yeah. I guess.

45
00:01:54.505 --> 00:01:56.551
Ah. so here. Stuart Scola.

46
00:01:56.594 --> 00:01:58.335
This is your new partner.Tiffany Wallace.

47
00:01:58.379 --> 00:01:59.858
- Oh.Nice to meet you.

48
00:01:59.902 --> 00:02:01.338
I thought you were startingnext week.

49
00:02:01.382 --> 00:02:02.992
- I got settled in a little
earlier than I thought.

50
00:02:03.035 --> 00:02:05.560
- Great. well. looking forward
to working with you.

51
00:02:05.603 --> 00:02:07.083
- Yeah. Tiffany spenttwo years in Atlanta

52
00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:09.781
working white-collar. but she
grew up here in Brooklyn.

53
00:02:09.825 --> 00:02:11.914
- Bed Stuy.
Thrilled to be back.

54
00:02:11.957 --> 00:02:14.090
- Oh. Tiffany. this is--
- Hey. I'm Omar.

55
00:02:14.134 --> 00:02:16.310
These guys call me "OA."

56
00:02:16.353 --> 00:02:18.399
- Okay. listen up.
I just got a call.

57
00:02:18.442 --> 00:02:20.096
There's been a mass shooting
in Greenpoint.

58
00:02:20.140 --> 00:02:21.489
I want all hands on deck.

59
00:02:21.532 --> 00:02:23.665
- Just like that.

60
00:02:23.708 --> 00:02:25.928
[soft dramatic music]

61
00:02:25.971 --> 00:02:31.977
♪

62
00:02:32.021 --> 00:02:34.154
- Maggie Bell.

63
00:02:34.197 --> 00:02:35.198
- [chuckles]
Hey.

64
00:02:35.242 --> 00:02:37.766
- You're back?
- Yeah. I am.

65
00:02:37.809 --> 00:02:40.421
We bump elbows or something?What are we doing?

66
00:02:40.464 --> 00:02:43.119
- No. I think we can hug.
- Right.

67
00:02:43.163 --> 00:02:44.947
- [chuckling]

68
00:02:44.990 --> 00:02:47.210
[soft music]

69
00:02:47.254 --> 00:02:49.386
Come on!

70
00:02:50.822 --> 00:02:52.650
- So how did the undercover
gig go?

71
00:02:52.694 --> 00:02:54.348
- Fine.

72
00:02:54.391 --> 00:02:57.133
- Did you close the case?
- I made 16 arrests.

73
00:02:57.177 --> 00:02:58.439
- Sounds like a home run.

74
00:02:58.482 --> 00:03:01.268
- Look. I'm just happy
to be back here with you.

75
00:03:01.311 --> 00:03:02.965
Playing "Maggie Bell" again.

76
00:03:03.008 --> 00:03:06.621
I mean. it's not as glamorous
pretending to be somebody 24/7.

77
00:03:06.664 --> 00:03:08.100
- But everything went well?

78
00:03:08.144 --> 00:03:10.407
- Got the job done.
- What does that mean?

79
00:03:10.451 --> 00:03:12.540
- It means that I'm ready
to move forward

80
00:03:12.583 --> 00:03:14.324
and start a new chapter.

81
00:03:15.847 --> 00:03:18.328
- Still need to be in control.
Copy that.

82
00:03:23.290 --> 00:03:26.510
- So. how'd you like
"Hotlanta"?

83
00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:29.470
- It was okay.

84
00:03:29.513 --> 00:03:33.952
A little too Southern for me.but I had fun.

85
00:03:33.996 --> 00:03:37.391
And just so you know. nobodycalls it "Hotlanta" anymore.

86
00:03:37.434 --> 00:03:39.044
- Oh.

87
00:03:39.088 --> 00:03:40.524
Got it.

88
00:03:40.568 --> 00:03:42.483
It's the first time
I ever said it. too.

89
00:03:44.224 --> 00:03:46.661
So why'd you leave NYPD?

90
00:03:46.704 --> 00:03:49.098
- Man. I feel like I'm
on a bad first date!

91
00:03:49.141 --> 00:03:51.753
- Oh.
Okay. I'm sorry.

92
00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:55.322
Didn't mean to...

93
00:03:55.365 --> 00:03:57.411
I thought "Hotlanta" would be
the most awkward moment

94
00:03:57.454 --> 00:03:58.586
of the morning.

95
00:03:58.629 --> 00:04:01.502
- Sorry. I'm just...

96
00:04:01.545 --> 00:04:04.809
sometimes I'm justa little bit too blunt.

97
00:04:04.853 --> 00:04:09.292
I left the NYPD
because I needed a change.

98
00:04:10.032 --> 00:04:12.339
I got tired of talkingabout the Yankees.

99
00:04:12.382 --> 00:04:15.298
the blue wall and hanging outat dive bars

100
00:04:15.342 --> 00:04:17.648
called O'Sullivan'sand Murphy's.

101
00:04:19.607 --> 00:04:21.913
- For the record.

102
00:04:21.957 --> 00:04:24.916
I'm half Irish.

103
00:04:31.271 --> 00:04:33.664
- Get a uniform to escort you.

104
00:04:33.708 --> 00:04:35.579
- Right over here.

105
00:04:35.623 --> 00:04:38.843
[indistinct chatter]

106
00:04:41.759 --> 00:04:43.761
- Maggie Bell.
- Tiffany Wallace.

107
00:04:43.805 --> 00:04:45.720
- Good to meet you.
- So what do we know?

108
00:04:45.763 --> 00:04:47.548
- We've got four dead.
all in their 20s.

109
00:04:47.591 --> 00:04:49.419
We've got two men. both white.

110
00:04:49.463 --> 00:04:51.334
Two women.
One white. one Asian.

111
00:04:51.378 --> 00:04:52.379
- Any witnesses?

112
00:04:52.422 --> 00:04:54.337
- A few. but theydidn't see much.

113
00:04:54.381 --> 00:04:55.338
The shooters
were wearing masks.

114
00:04:55.382 --> 00:04:56.731
- We recover the casings?

115
00:04:56.774 --> 00:04:58.385
- Yeah. we know the shooters
were using Krinkovs.

116
00:04:58.428 --> 00:04:59.603
- Have you found
the shooters yet?

117
00:04:59.647 --> 00:05:00.996
- Excuse me. sir.
can you back up?

118
00:05:01.039 --> 00:05:02.302
- This is my company.

119
00:05:02.345 --> 00:05:03.912
Those four people in body bagsare my employees.

120
00:05:03.955 --> 00:05:05.261
I have a right to knowwhat's going on.

121
00:05:05.305 --> 00:05:07.742
- You're absolutely right.
Let's take a walk.

122
00:05:07.785 --> 00:05:10.266
We'll find a quiet place
we can talk.

123
00:05:10.310 --> 00:05:12.007
♪

124
00:05:12.050 --> 00:05:13.748
- All right. come on in!
Just talked to Maggie.

125
00:05:13.791 --> 00:05:15.010
Here's what we know so far.

126
00:05:15.053 --> 00:05:17.273
We got two shooters.
both firing Krinkovs.

127
00:05:17.317 --> 00:05:20.668
Four victims. all journalists
at Echt Media.

128
00:05:20.711 --> 00:05:23.148
- Known for its progressive
political commentary

129
00:05:23.192 --> 00:05:25.107
and disruptive social ideas.

130
00:05:25.150 --> 00:05:26.717
- Right.
They're liberal--most likely

131
00:05:26.761 --> 00:05:28.589
extremely liberal. which means
we need to start digging

132
00:05:28.632 --> 00:05:30.025
into right-wing hate groups.

133
00:05:30.068 --> 00:05:32.332
Pull security cam footage
within a two-block radius.

134
00:05:32.375 --> 00:05:34.812
Get to work. let's talk
to each other. people!

135
00:05:34.856 --> 00:05:35.813
- Hey.

136
00:05:35.857 --> 00:05:37.119
So Maggie and OAare on the scene.

137
00:05:37.162 --> 00:05:38.860
Scola and Tiffanyare canvassing for witnesses.

138
00:05:38.903 --> 00:05:41.297
but so far no actionable leads.

139
00:05:41.341 --> 00:05:42.603
But dock is hot. so...

140
00:05:42.646 --> 00:05:45.170
- Great. thanks.
- Yeah.

141
00:05:45.214 --> 00:05:46.955
Oh. hey. uh...

142
00:05:48.609 --> 00:05:50.915
Got a text from Kristen.She's moving to Dallas. huh?

143
00:05:50.959 --> 00:05:52.003
- Yeah.

144
00:05:52.047 --> 00:05:54.354
Yeah. she wanted
a change of scenery.

145
00:05:54.397 --> 00:05:56.007
It's her decision.

146
00:05:56.051 --> 00:05:57.879
- Right.

147
00:05:57.922 --> 00:06:00.621
Okay. well... as long
as she's happy. I guess.

148
00:06:00.664 --> 00:06:03.275
- She is.

149
00:06:05.147 --> 00:06:07.018
- I wasn't awareof any specific threats.

150
00:06:07.062 --> 00:06:09.412
but we do get hundreds ofnon-specific threats every day.

151
00:06:09.456 --> 00:06:10.761
- Well. what do you mean
by that?

152
00:06:10.805 --> 00:06:12.633
- Well. there's so much hatein the air.

153
00:06:12.676 --> 00:06:14.069
No matter what you say.the other side is constantly

154
00:06:14.112 --> 00:06:16.158
on the attack.
and it's personal.

155
00:06:16.201 --> 00:06:18.639
You know. it used to be all
this political and social

156
00:06:18.682 --> 00:06:20.336
vitriol was just rhetoric.

157
00:06:20.380 --> 00:06:22.730
Now it's like we are actually
on the verge of a civil war.

158
00:06:22.773 --> 00:06:24.253
- Well. have you posted
anything controversial

159
00:06:24.296 --> 00:06:25.646
the past few days?

160
00:06:25.689 --> 00:06:27.822
Anything that would agitate
a certain political

161
00:06:27.865 --> 00:06:29.693
or ethnic group?
- It's our goal to publish

162
00:06:29.737 --> 00:06:31.391
something controversial
every day.

163
00:06:31.434 --> 00:06:32.914
It's our business model.

164
00:06:32.957 --> 00:06:35.177
I'm happy to answerany other questions you have.

165
00:06:35.220 --> 00:06:36.526
but I should go.

166
00:06:36.570 --> 00:06:37.832
I need to talk
to the employees.

167
00:06:37.875 --> 00:06:40.487
- Okay. sir. that's not how--
- Hey.

168
00:06:40.530 --> 00:06:41.488
Just got a textfrom my informant.

169
00:06:41.531 --> 00:06:42.706
He may have a lead.

170
00:06:47.407 --> 00:06:49.974
- You guys out here
when the shooting went down?

171
00:06:50.018 --> 00:06:51.411
[whistles]
Excuse me.

172
00:06:51.454 --> 00:06:53.891
I asked you a question.
- Yeah. I ain't answering.

173
00:06:54.936 --> 00:06:56.198
- Did you hear
any gunshots. sir?

174
00:06:56.241 --> 00:06:58.896
- Man. you deaf?
I just said I ain't talking!

175
00:06:58.940 --> 00:07:01.551
- You ain't talking. why?
'Cause you're a tough guy?

176
00:07:01.595 --> 00:07:03.118
- 'Cause you're the police.

177
00:07:03.161 --> 00:07:05.294
- No. we're the FBI.

178
00:07:05.337 --> 00:07:06.687
So let me ask you again.

179
00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:07.862
Were you out here
when the shooting went down?

180
00:07:07.905 --> 00:07:10.299
Yes or no?
- No.

181
00:07:10.342 --> 00:07:12.040
- Aw. look at you.

182
00:07:12.083 --> 00:07:13.824
Trying to be all hard
and make a statement.

183
00:07:13.868 --> 00:07:15.783
- You don't know a damn
thing about me. lady.

184
00:07:15.826 --> 00:07:18.307
- One. don't call me "lady."

185
00:07:18.350 --> 00:07:20.918
Two. I know a lot about you.

186
00:07:20.962 --> 00:07:24.226
Like that tattoo on your arm?
"BMW"?

187
00:07:24.269 --> 00:07:26.446
Means you roll
with Brooklyn's Most Wanted.

188
00:07:26.489 --> 00:07:28.317
which means you're connected
to the Trey-Nine Crips.

189
00:07:28.360 --> 00:07:30.798
which means you probably
grew up in Brownsville.

190
00:07:30.841 --> 00:07:34.192
I'm guessing the Tilden Street
Housing Projects.

191
00:07:34.236 --> 00:07:35.933
♪

192
00:07:35.977 --> 00:07:39.415
Another thing you should know.
Jalen.

193
00:07:39.459 --> 00:07:42.244
is that lying to me ain't like
lying to some fat dude

194
00:07:42.287 --> 00:07:44.289
in a blue uniform.

195
00:07:44.333 --> 00:07:45.900
It's a felony.

196
00:07:45.943 --> 00:07:48.293
You do time behind that crap.

197
00:07:50.382 --> 00:07:51.862
So the second
I walk away from here.

198
00:07:51.906 --> 00:07:53.255
I'ma pull every piece
of surveillance footage

199
00:07:53.298 --> 00:07:54.691
I can find.

200
00:07:54.735 --> 00:07:57.477
And if I see your sorry butt
out here at 8:27 a.m..

201
00:07:57.520 --> 00:07:59.130
I'ma charge you with perjury.

202
00:07:59.174 --> 00:08:01.785
- Wait. wait. wait. wait.
Wait.

203
00:08:01.829 --> 00:08:03.570
Look. I was here.

204
00:08:03.613 --> 00:08:06.224
I--I heard the gunshots.
- Then what?

205
00:08:06.268 --> 00:08:10.098
- I saw two dudes wearing masks
jump into a blue car.

206
00:08:10.141 --> 00:08:12.317
- What kind of car?
- I'm not sure.

207
00:08:12.361 --> 00:08:15.799
A sedan?
Kia. maybe?

208
00:08:17.148 --> 00:08:20.151
- It was nice doing business
with you. Jalen.

209
00:08:20.195 --> 00:08:23.154
[dramatic music]

210
00:08:23.198 --> 00:08:26.854
♪

211
00:08:26.897 --> 00:08:28.420
- Nice work back there.

212
00:08:28.464 --> 00:08:30.118
But you didn't need
to jump in like that.

213
00:08:30.161 --> 00:08:32.512
I had everything under control.

214
00:08:32.555 --> 00:08:34.209
- Oh. my bad.

215
00:08:34.252 --> 00:08:36.037
I just reacted.

216
00:08:36.080 --> 00:08:39.780
I knew who that dude was. what
buttons to press. so I did it.

217
00:08:39.823 --> 00:08:41.259
But I'm sorry
if I offended you.

218
00:08:41.303 --> 00:08:42.478
- No big deal.

219
00:08:42.522 --> 00:08:44.959
Just thought I'd. you know...say something.

220
00:08:45.002 --> 00:08:46.613
- I'm glad you did.

221
00:08:46.656 --> 00:08:48.745
But for the record. Scola...

222
00:08:48.789 --> 00:08:50.747
if you got a problem
with people speaking up.

223
00:08:50.791 --> 00:08:52.575
if you got a lot of rules
about when and how

224
00:08:52.619 --> 00:08:55.926
I'm supposed to talk to people.
you should let me know.

225
00:08:55.970 --> 00:08:59.843
Now.
'Cause I don't roll like that.

226
00:08:59.887 --> 00:09:01.758
- Well. neither do I.

227
00:09:01.802 --> 00:09:04.369
So you got nothing
to worry about.

228
00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:09.157
And I'd preferif you call me "Stuart."

229
00:09:10.506 --> 00:09:12.987
- I'll let Jubal know
about the blue Kia.

230
00:09:16.556 --> 00:09:17.774
- Hey.

231
00:09:17.818 --> 00:09:19.384
- I'm sorry to bother you. man.

232
00:09:19.428 --> 00:09:23.911
But I'm just--
I'm sorta freaking.

233
00:09:23.954 --> 00:09:25.913
I was working last nightat that biker bar.

234
00:09:25.956 --> 00:09:27.305
I was talking to these twodudes I know.

235
00:09:27.349 --> 00:09:30.308
I've been working real hardthe past few weeks!

236
00:09:30.352 --> 00:09:33.660
Anyway. they start talkingabout doing some crazy stuff.

237
00:09:33.703 --> 00:09:35.009
Okay?Um...

238
00:09:35.052 --> 00:09:36.271
"Making noise."They kept saying that.

239
00:09:36.314 --> 00:09:38.316
"We're gonna makesome noise. bro."

240
00:09:38.360 --> 00:09:39.796
I tried to find out what theywere talking about. but--

241
00:09:39.840 --> 00:09:41.842
- You know these guys' names?

242
00:09:41.885 --> 00:09:43.278
- Tyler and Eddie.

243
00:09:43.321 --> 00:09:44.714
I don't know their last names.Didn't ask.

244
00:09:44.758 --> 00:09:46.673
You told me. "Never askfor last names.

245
00:09:46.716 --> 00:09:49.371
They'll think you're a cop."

246
00:09:49.414 --> 00:09:51.199
[coughing]

247
00:09:51.242 --> 00:09:52.809
I think it's possible thoseguys might have been involved

248
00:09:52.853 --> 00:09:54.245
in that shooting this morning.

249
00:09:54.289 --> 00:09:55.856
- What do you mean. "involved"?

250
00:09:55.899 --> 00:09:58.641
- The guy who drove the car...

251
00:09:58.685 --> 00:10:00.904
he was at the bar this morning.

252
00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:04.734
- What the hell
are you talking about?

253
00:10:04.778 --> 00:10:06.344
- He came by the bar
an hour ago.

254
