759
00:29:51.398 --> 00:29:54.488
Scola. head over
to 14 165th Street now.

760
00:29:54.531 --> 00:29:57.970
Ellis is gonna attack
Trans For Life.

761
00:29:58.013 --> 00:30:00.015
- Trans For Life office
is over there.

762
00:30:00.059 --> 00:30:01.800
SWAT's clearing the building
as we speak.

763
00:30:01.843 --> 00:30:03.802
- Are we sure Ellis is actuallyhere in the vicinity?

764
00:30:03.845 --> 00:30:05.673
- According to Jubal.
the last visual contact

765
00:30:05.716 --> 00:30:08.067
was at 163rd and Riverside.

766
00:30:08.110 --> 00:30:09.459
- Probably found
a place to park.

767
00:30:09.503 --> 00:30:10.939
which means he's on foot
walking north

768
00:30:10.983 --> 00:30:12.201
towards the office building.

769
00:30:12.245 --> 00:30:15.291
I'll go east. you go west.

770
00:30:15.335 --> 00:30:18.468
[suspenseful music]

771
00:30:18.512 --> 00:30:25.432
♪

772
00:30:31.133 --> 00:30:32.918
- I got eyes
on Ellis's vehicle.

773
00:30:32.961 --> 00:30:35.659
It's parked on the south side
of 162nd.

774
00:30:35.703 --> 00:30:41.056
Exact address is 122 162nd.

775
00:30:41.100 --> 00:30:45.931
♪

776
00:30:45.974 --> 00:30:48.411
Car's empty. and I want a bomb
team out here right away.

777
00:30:48.455 --> 00:30:51.023
This thing could be rigged.

778
00:30:51.066 --> 00:30:52.894
[phone ringing]

779
00:30:52.938 --> 00:30:55.288
- Hey. what's going on?
- Any sign of William?

780
00:30:55.331 --> 00:30:57.812
- No. I haven't seen him.
But what's up with that SUV?

781
00:30:57.856 --> 00:30:59.770
- It's clean. but the dogs
detected chemicals.

782
00:30:59.814 --> 00:31:01.337
so it's likely a bomb
was in the vehicle

783
00:31:01.381 --> 00:31:04.079
within the past hour or so.
meaning...

784
00:31:04.123 --> 00:31:05.472
- Ellis is carrying it.

785
00:31:05.515 --> 00:31:07.648
- We also found a pamphlet
for another charity.

786
00:31:07.691 --> 00:31:10.651
It's "Black and Proud NYC"
on Broadway.

787
00:31:10.694 --> 00:31:12.479
Could be we're chasing
the wrong target.

788
00:31:12.522 --> 00:31:15.003
- Okay. I'm heading west now.
- Okay. good.

789
00:31:15.047 --> 00:31:16.831
I'm sending the SWAT team
there now to evacuate.

790
00:31:16.875 --> 00:31:18.354
- Hold up.

791
00:31:20.139 --> 00:31:21.531
I see him.

792
00:31:21.575 --> 00:31:23.229
He's wearing blue jeans.
a tan jacket.

793
00:31:23.272 --> 00:31:24.883
and he's carrying
a blue backpack.

794
00:31:24.926 --> 00:31:26.362
- Okay. wait for backup.

795
00:31:26.406 --> 00:31:28.147
- He's headed towards
the building. the target.

796
00:31:28.190 --> 00:31:30.627
- Okay. okay.
I'm sending a team to you now.

797
00:31:30.671 --> 00:31:33.761
♪

798
00:31:33.804 --> 00:31:35.502
- William Ellis!
FBI.

799
00:31:35.545 --> 00:31:38.374
Stop walking.
I said stop walking!

800
00:31:38.418 --> 00:31:39.898
Are you sure there's a bomb
in that backpack?

801
00:31:39.941 --> 00:31:41.247
'Cause this dude
is not complying.

802
00:31:41.290 --> 00:31:43.510
- Yes. I told you.
the dog got a chemical hit.

803
00:31:43.553 --> 00:31:45.642
- I've had dogs alert
to bubble gum. bruh.

804
00:31:45.686 --> 00:31:47.122
What I'm asking is.
is the dog good?

805
00:31:47.166 --> 00:31:48.515
Can I trust him?
- Yes.

806
00:31:48.558 --> 00:31:50.212
- Are you sure?
- Trust me.

807
00:31:50.256 --> 00:31:51.648
[disconnect tone]

808
00:31:52.998 --> 00:31:54.173
- William Ellis!

809
00:31:54.216 --> 00:31:55.914
Put your hands up
and stop walking!

810
00:31:55.957 --> 00:31:58.090
I will not ask again!

811
00:31:58.133 --> 00:32:05.227
♪

812
00:32:14.410 --> 00:32:16.891
- [heavy breathing]

813
00:32:16.935 --> 00:32:19.981
[tense music]

814
00:32:20.025 --> 00:32:27.119
♪

815
00:32:30.383 --> 00:32:31.862
- Backpack is hot.

816
00:32:31.906 --> 00:32:33.212
Going to try and defuse it.

817
00:32:33.255 --> 00:32:35.954
- I told you that dog was good.

818
00:32:35.997 --> 00:32:38.869
- I know.

819
00:32:38.913 --> 00:32:40.741
Thanks.

820
00:32:42.308 --> 00:32:44.092
- Good news--
we just took Ellis down.

821
00:32:44.136 --> 00:32:45.485
He was pronounced dead
at the scene.

822
00:32:45.528 --> 00:32:47.443
He had a pipe bomb
in his backpack.

823
00:32:47.487 --> 00:32:48.836
- Okay.

824
00:32:48.879 --> 00:32:51.273
It means our friend Zayne
is no longer an asset.

825
00:32:51.317 --> 00:32:53.449
Keep talking to him.
Make him comfortable.

826
00:32:53.493 --> 00:32:54.755
And then lure him to the window

827
00:32:54.798 --> 00:32:57.105
on the southwest side
of the café.

828
00:32:57.149 --> 00:32:58.802
Tell him there's an SUVthere waiting for him.

829
00:32:58.846 --> 00:33:01.153
- No. I can't do that.
- I'm not asking.

830
00:33:01.196 --> 00:33:02.981
- He's my informant.
my friend.

831
00:33:03.024 --> 00:33:05.635
- Yeah. but how he's taken
seven people hostage.

832
00:33:13.992 --> 00:33:15.602
- I'll go inside.

833
00:33:15.645 --> 00:33:17.691
If I talk to him in person.
I can get him to surrender.

834
00:33:17.734 --> 00:33:19.258
- That's a really dumb idea.
- Yeah. well.

835
00:33:19.301 --> 00:33:20.520
it's a hell of a lot better
than trying to take him out

836
00:33:20.563 --> 00:33:22.348
with a sniper rifle
from 50 yards.

837
00:33:22.391 --> 00:33:23.958
What if you miss. huh?

838
00:33:24.002 --> 00:33:27.179
He'll snap and light up every
single person in that café.

839
00:33:28.484 --> 00:33:30.443
- Stand down. Zidan.

840
00:33:30.486 --> 00:33:32.488
Hey. you going in there
elevates the risk!

841
00:33:32.532 --> 00:33:35.100
- Yeah. for me.
Not the hostages.

842
00:33:35.143 --> 00:33:36.971
- You're too close
to this guy.

843
00:33:37.015 --> 00:33:38.277
- No.

844
00:33:38.320 --> 00:33:41.889
I can do this.
and I know what's at stake.

845
00:33:41.932 --> 00:33:45.893
[somber music]

846
00:33:45.936 --> 00:33:48.765
And. if necessary. I will take
him out in a heartbeat.

847
00:33:50.115 --> 00:33:52.813
- Nestor?

848
00:33:52.856 --> 00:33:55.207
♪

849
00:33:55.250 --> 00:33:58.079
Give him a shot.Let him do his thing.

850
00:33:58.123 --> 00:34:01.082
If OA says he can do it.he can do it.

851
00:34:01.126 --> 00:34:03.258
You can trust me.

852
00:34:03.302 --> 00:34:06.870
♪

853
00:34:06.914 --> 00:34:09.482
- You have five minutes.
then I'm doing it my way.

854
00:34:09.525 --> 00:34:12.746
Anyone dies. anyone gets hurt.
it's on you.

855
00:34:15.009 --> 00:34:17.925
[suspenseful music]

856
00:34:17.968 --> 00:34:23.148
♪

857
00:34:23.191 --> 00:34:24.975
- Zayne.
I'm coming in!

858
00:34:25.019 --> 00:34:26.803
- That's not a good idea.

859
00:34:26.847 --> 00:34:28.153
- Yeah. I know.

860
00:34:28.196 --> 00:34:30.546
A lot people seem to feel
that way. too.

861
00:34:30.590 --> 00:34:32.983
But I'm gonna go ahead
and come in anyway. all right?

862
00:34:33.027 --> 00:34:35.769
- No. Omar.
Don't!

863
00:34:35.812 --> 00:34:38.250
- It's just me.

864
00:34:38.293 --> 00:34:39.599
- Okay?
It's just me.

865
00:34:39.642 --> 00:34:43.559
- So calm down.
We're gonna figure this out.

866
00:34:44.386 --> 00:34:45.822
- Put your gun down.

867
00:34:45.866 --> 00:34:47.389
- Okay. okay.

868
00:34:47.433 --> 00:34:54.570
♪

869
00:34:55.789 --> 00:34:59.009
Now you put yours down--
it's only fair.

870
00:34:59.053 --> 00:35:02.187
- No.
It doesn't work that way.

871
00:35:02.230 --> 00:35:03.710
- Okay. fine.

872
00:35:03.753 --> 00:35:05.712
I know you're not
gonna hurt me.

873
00:35:05.755 --> 00:35:07.279
And I know you're not gonna
hurt those people.

874
00:35:07.322 --> 00:35:08.802
because you are a good kid.
Zayne.

875
00:35:08.845 --> 00:35:10.543
- Quit playing me. Omar!

876
00:35:10.586 --> 00:35:11.892
- Why do you keep saying that?

877
00:35:11.935 --> 00:35:14.721
Zayne. I have never
lied to you ever.

878
00:35:14.764 --> 00:35:16.157
- Really?

879
00:35:16.201 --> 00:35:18.028
You lied to me earlier today.

880
00:35:19.465 --> 00:35:21.336
- What are you talking about?

881
00:35:21.380 --> 00:35:23.338
- You never texted your friend
at the FBI.

882
00:35:23.382 --> 00:35:25.166
That was just a bunch of crap

883
00:35:25.210 --> 00:35:27.168
to get me investedin the mission!

884
00:35:27.212 --> 00:35:29.736
You're just using me!

885
00:35:31.129 --> 00:35:33.305
Yeah.

886
00:35:33.348 --> 00:35:35.524
Show me your phone.

887
00:35:35.568 --> 00:35:38.310
Yeah. I want to see the text.

888
00:35:38.353 --> 00:35:40.877
Come on.

889
00:35:40.921 --> 00:35:42.314
Or. you know what?

890
00:35:42.357 --> 00:35:44.403
You. big guy.
Get up.

891
00:35:44.446 --> 00:35:47.145
Come right over here.

892
00:35:47.188 --> 00:35:50.060
And get on your knees.

893
00:35:50.104 --> 00:35:52.106
Omar. I swear to God.

894
00:35:52.150 --> 00:35:54.630
show me your phone
or I'm gonna shoot this guy.

895
00:35:54.674 --> 00:35:56.806
- Prepare to engage.
- Yes. sir.

896
00:35:56.850 --> 00:35:57.807
He's on me.

897
00:35:57.851 --> 00:36:00.419
♪

898
00:36:00.462 --> 00:36:02.072
- Come on!

899
00:36:03.248 --> 00:36:06.251
- Okay. okay.

900
00:36:06.294 --> 00:36:08.383
You wanna do this your way?

901
00:36:08.427 --> 00:36:14.215
♪

902
00:36:14.259 --> 00:36:17.914
Okay.
It's there. take it.

903
00:36:18.872 --> 00:36:22.963
You're gonna have to scroll.
The name is "Robert Harper."

904
00:36:23.006 --> 00:36:27.228
♪

905
00:36:27.272 --> 00:36:30.013
Keep going.

906
00:36:30.057 --> 00:36:33.365
♪

907
00:36:33.408 --> 00:36:34.975
- I. uh...

908
00:36:35.018 --> 00:36:38.239
♪

909
00:36:38.283 --> 00:36:40.415
You really texted him?

910
00:36:40.459 --> 00:36:46.291
♪

911
00:36:46.334 --> 00:36:49.511
- Yeah. man.
Come on.

912
00:36:50.469 --> 00:36:53.123
- I'm sorry.
Uh...

913
00:36:54.690 --> 00:36:56.997
I'm not--I'm not thinking
so good.

914
00:36:57.040 --> 00:36:58.259
- I know.

915
00:36:58.303 --> 00:37:01.828
So put the gun down
and let these people go.

916
00:37:01.871 --> 00:37:03.525
and you and me
are gonna figure this out.

917
00:37:03.569 --> 00:37:06.528
You have my word. Zayne.

918
00:37:06.572 --> 00:37:10.140
Come on. Zayne.
Put it down.

919
00:37:10.184 --> 00:37:11.446
Please. put it down.

920
00:37:11.490 --> 00:37:15.276
♪

921
00:37:15.320 --> 00:37:18.279
- [crying]

922
00:37:18.323 --> 00:37:20.150
- Go. go.

923
00:37:20.194 --> 00:37:21.587
Guys!

924
00:37:21.630 --> 00:37:24.416
[somber music]

925
00:37:24.459 --> 00:37:26.896
♪

926
00:37:26.940 --> 00:37:29.290
- [crying]

927
00:37:29.334 --> 00:37:33.903
♪

928
00:37:35.862 --> 00:37:39.213
- [sighs]
What the hell. Zayne?

929
00:37:39.257 --> 00:37:42.260
♪

930
00:37:42.303 --> 00:37:46.438
- [crying]

931
00:37:46.481 --> 00:37:53.096
♪

932
00:37:53.140 --> 00:37:55.142
- Told you he'd get it done.

933
00:37:55.185 --> 00:37:56.535
- Yeah. he did.

934
00:37:56.578 --> 00:37:58.058
But you put mein a bad position.

935
00:37:58.101 --> 00:37:59.233
- Oh. how's that?

936
00:37:59.277 --> 00:38:01.235
- I didn't needanother opinion to process

937
00:38:01.279 --> 00:38:03.019
at that particularmoment in time.

938
00:38:03.063 --> 00:38:05.544
- I know. it was a very
stressful situation.

939
00:38:05.587 --> 00:38:08.198
But you know that I'm only ever
trying to get the best result.

940
00:38:08.242 --> 00:38:10.853
- I know.

941
00:38:10.897 --> 00:38:12.899
I know. okay.I'll see you in a few?

942
00:38:12.942 --> 00:38:16.424
- Yeah. right.
The medal ceremony.

943
00:38:16.468 --> 00:38:18.426
- It's gonna be great.
come on.

944
00:38:18.470 --> 00:38:20.863
- It's not funny!
- Don't beat yourself up.

945
00:38:20.907 --> 00:38:23.605
Things happen.
Things out of our control.

946
00:38:23.649 --> 00:38:25.215
It's part of the job.
- Yeah. I know that.

947
00:38:25.259 --> 00:38:27.217
- Okay. so when
the ADIC calls your name.

948
00:38:27.261 --> 00:38:30.569
walk up there
with a proud smile on your face

949
00:38:30.612 --> 00:38:33.485
and grab that damn medal.

950
00:38:33.528 --> 00:38:35.530
Okay?

951
00:38:35.574 --> 00:38:37.793
'Cause you deserve it.

952
00:38:40.753 --> 00:38:43.930
Without you. we never would
have made that case.

953
00:38:46.976 --> 00:38:49.196
- Thank you.

954
00:38:49.239 --> 00:38:52.155
[soft dramatic music]

955
00:38:52.199 --> 00:38:59.162
♪

956
00:39:03.166 --> 00:39:06.039
Okay.

957
00:39:06.082 --> 00:39:09.912
♪

958
00:39:09.956 --> 00:39:12.959
See you later.
- Bye.

959
00:39:13.002 --> 00:39:14.700
- Do you need any help
with the paperwork?

960
00:39:14.743 --> 00:39:16.310
- [sighs]
No. I got it.

961
00:39:16.354 --> 00:39:17.964
New guy does the paperwork.

962
00:39:18.007 --> 00:39:20.227
Don't worry. I know the rules.

963
00:39:22.534 --> 00:39:24.710
I punched my lieutenant
in the face.

964
00:39:29.932 --> 00:39:32.674
That's the reason
I left the NYPD.

965
00:39:36.939 --> 00:39:38.419
- Oh.

966
00:39:38.463 --> 00:39:41.161
- He was drunk and he said
something pretty disgusting.

967
00:39:41.204 --> 00:39:43.424
so I hit him.

968
00:39:43.468 --> 00:39:45.861
I got him good. too.

969
00:39:45.905 --> 00:39:48.429
A couple months later.
an ASAC I know

970
00:39:48.473 --> 00:39:49.648
asked me
if I would be interested

971
00:39:49.691 --> 00:39:52.564
in working with the FBI.
so I jumped.

972
00:39:52.607 --> 00:39:59.745
♪

973
00:40:02.530 --> 00:40:04.271
See you tomorrow.

974
00:40:04.314 --> 00:40:10.277
♪

975
00:40:10.320 --> 00:40:11.844
- Well. look at you.

976
00:40:11.887 --> 00:40:14.107
- Hey. [chuckles]
Uh. yeah.

977
00:40:14.150 --> 00:40:16.239
I'm. uh. gussied up.

978
00:40:16.283 --> 00:40:19.068
- I don't know what that means.
- It just means I'm dressed up.

979
00:40:19.112 --> 00:40:22.202
I'm. um. getting
a gold medal tonight

980
00:40:22.245 --> 00:40:25.553
for my extraordinary
and courageous efforts

981
00:40:25.597 --> 00:40:28.948
in connection
with Operation Powder. so...

982
00:40:28.991 --> 00:40:31.124
- Well. congratulations.That's amazing.

983
00:40:31.167 --> 00:40:32.517
- Thanks. yeah.

984
00:40:32.560 --> 00:40:34.432
- Before you go. though. um...

985
00:40:34.475 --> 00:40:38.261
I wanted to thank you forstanding up for me with Nestor.

986
00:40:38.305 --> 00:40:41.569
It really meant a lot.
- Of course.

987
00:40:41.613 --> 00:40:44.006
I'm just really glad
that it worked out.

988
00:40:44.050 --> 00:40:46.835
You know. I could see that
it was hard for you.

989
00:40:46.879 --> 00:40:49.229
You clearly care about Zayne.

990
00:40:49.272 --> 00:40:52.101
Probably tough to watch him
blow up his life like that.

991
00:40:54.190 --> 00:40:55.801
- It is what it is.

992
00:40:58.673 --> 00:41:02.242
- I don't want to be late.
- Go. go. I'll see you there!

993
00:41:05.811 --> 00:41:07.247
- You're coming?
- Oh. yeah.

994
00:41:07.290 --> 00:41:09.771
It's not every day that my
partner gets a gold medal.

995
00:41:12.295 --> 00:41:14.036
- Okay.

996
00:41:14.080 --> 00:41:16.082
- Okay. what's going on
with you?

997
00:41:16.125 --> 00:41:18.737
- What?
- Why are you so unexcited?

998
00:41:18.780 --> 00:41:19.825
The operation
was a huge success.

999
00:41:19.868 --> 00:41:22.436
You arrested 16 people.

1000
00:41:22.480 --> 00:41:25.526
- Yeah. that's true.

1001
00:41:25.570 --> 00:41:27.615
We also killed someone.

1002
00:41:28.616 --> 00:41:31.445
Her name was Anna.Um...

1003
00:41:32.185 --> 00:41:34.448
She was married
to one of the targets.

1004
00:41:34.492 --> 00:41:37.059
She had just turned 22.

1005
00:41:37.103 --> 00:41:38.713
You know. I'd spent a lot
of time with her

1006
00:41:38.757 --> 00:41:40.628
and I considered her a friend.

1007
00:41:42.412 --> 00:41:47.287
The day of the arrest.
she panicked.

1008
00:41:47.330 --> 00:41:48.506
And she grabbed a knife

1009
00:41:48.549 --> 00:41:51.683
and she ran
towards one of the officers.

1010
00:41:51.726 --> 00:41:54.207
[melancholy music]

1011
00:41:54.250 --> 00:41:57.340
I shot her.

1012
00:41:57.384 --> 00:42:00.213
I didn't have a choice.

1013
00:42:00.256 --> 00:42:02.215
[sighs]

1014
00:42:02.258 --> 00:42:07.176
But we made 16 arrests. right?
So that's what matters.

1015
00:42:09.004 --> 00:42:13.095
I really should go.
I don't want to be late.

1016
00:42:13.139 --> 00:42:16.316
Like you said. not every day
you get a gold medal. right?

1017
00:42:16.359 --> 00:42:23.323
♪

1018
00:42:40.819 --> 00:42:43.735
